{brightCyan,bold}Arch Linux Beginner Notes{/}
{cyan}═══════════════════════════{/}

{brightYellow,bold}Initial Setup & Customisation{/}
{yellow}─────────────────────────────────{/}
{green}□{/} Install yay (AUR helper): {cyan}git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/yay.git && cd yay && makepkg -si{/}
{green}□{/} Update system: {cyan}sudo pacman -Syu{/}
{green}□{/} Install essential packages: {cyan}sudo pacman -S vim git htop neofetch{/}
{green}□{/} Configure .bashrc with aliases and PS1 customization
{green}□{/} Install and configure zsh with oh-my-zsh
{green}□{/} Set up dotfiles repository for configuration management

{brightYellow,bold}Desktop Environment & Window Manager{/}
{yellow}───────────────────────────────────────{/}
{green}□{/} Install i3wm: {cyan}sudo pacman -S i3-wm i3status i3lock dmenu{/}
{green}□{/} Configure i3 config file: {blue}~/.config/i3/config{/}
{green}□{/} Install polybar for better status bar
{green}□{/} Set up rofi as application launcher
{green}□{/} Configure picom for transparency and effects
{green}□{/} Install and configure nitrogen for wallpapers

{brightYellow,bold}Cron Jobs & Automation{/}
{yellow}─────────────────────────{/}
{green}□{/} Edit crontab: {cyan}crontab -e{/}
{green}□{/} System updates: {purple}0 2 * * 0{/} {cyan}yay -Syu --noconfirm{/}
{green}□{/} Backup home directory: {purple}0 3 * * 1{/} {cyan}rsync -av /home/user/ /backup/{/}
{green}□{/} Clean package cache: {purple}0 4 * * *{/} {cyan}paccache -r{/}
{green}□{/} Check disk usage: {purple}0 9 * * *{/} {cyan}df -h | mail -s "Disk Usage" user@localhost{/}

{brightRed,bold}Common Errors & Solutions{/}
{red}────────────────────────────{/}

{brightWhite,bold}1.{/} {red}"error: failed to commit transaction (conflicting files)"{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} {cyan}sudo pacman -S --overwrite '*' package-name{/}

{brightWhite,bold}2.{/} {red}"error: could not lock database"{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} {cyan}sudo rm /var/lib/pacman/db.lck{/}

{brightWhite,bold}3.{/} {red}"error: target not found"{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} {cyan}sudo pacman -Sy{/} then retry installation

{brightWhite,bold}4.{/} {red}AUR package build fails{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} Check dependencies, install base-devel group

{brightWhite,bold}5.{/} {red}"No space left on device"{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} Clean package cache with {cyan}paccache -r{/}, remove orphaned packages

{brightWhite,bold}6.{/} {red}X11 won't start after update{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} Check Xorg logs, reinstall graphics drivers

{brightWhite,bold}7.{/} {red}Sound not working{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} Install {cyan}alsa-utils{/}, run {cyan}alsamixer{/}, unmute channels

{brightWhite,bold}8.{/} {red}Network issues after boot{/}
   {green,bold}Solution:{/} Enable NetworkManager: {cyan}sudo systemctl enable NetworkManager{/}

{brightBlue,bold}Useful Commands{/}
{blue}──────────────────{/}
{white}•{/} List installed packages: {cyan}pacman -Q{/}
{white}•{/} Find package files: {cyan}pacman -Ql package-name{/}
{white}•{/} Search for package: {cyan}pacman -Ss search-term{/}
{white}•{/} Remove orphaned packages: {cyan}sudo pacman -Rns $(pacman -Qtdq){/}
{white}•{/} Check system logs: {cyan}journalctl -xe{/}
{white}•{/} Monitor system resources: {cyan}htop{/}
{white}•{/} Check running services: {cyan}systemctl list-units --type=service{/}

{brightPurple,bold}Tips for Beginners{/}
{purple}─────────────────────{/}
{white}•{/} Always read the {brightCyan}Arch Wiki{/} before making changes
{white}•{/} Keep a backup of working configurations
{white}•{/} Test new configurations in a virtual machine first
{white}•{/} Join the Arch Linux forums and IRC for help
{white}•{/} Use {cyan}timeshift{/} for system snapshots
{white}•{/} {red,bold}Don't run random commands from the internet without understanding them{/}
